    "result_text": "Full suite green: **278 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` flag on owner creation, following the existing `namesakeCount` (cp16) pattern of a `@Transient` field computed by a pipeline step before save.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `sharesHousehold` boolean property (readOnly) to the `Owner` response schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field. MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean sharesHousehold` field with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`AssignSharesHousehold.java`** (new function) \u2014 runs before save, so `findAll()` returns only pre-existing owners; sets `sharesHousehold = true` when any existing owner has the same address **and** city, else `false`. Creation always proceeds.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignSharesHousehold` step (under `transaction` governance) into the pipeline between `assignNamesakeCount` and `save`.\n\nThe cp17 test passes (first owner at an address \u2192 `false`, second at the same address+city \u2192 `true`), cp16 still passes, and the full suite is green.",
